 About: Processes                                                     
   PID             Process ID, a number the OS gives each running     
                   process. Use it with `syscope kill <pid>`. IDs are 
                   reused after a process exits.                      
   NAME            The program's executable name. Grouping (z)        
                   combines processes with the same name, e.g.        
                   "chrome (31)", summing their CPU and memory. The   
                   tree (t) nests each process under the one that     
                   started it. ▸ can be expanded with l, ▾ collapsed  
                   with h. (suspended) is paused (p resumes it);      
                   (exited) has ended but its parent hasn't cleaned   
                   it up yet.                                         
   USER            The account the process runs as. Blank usually     
